szcompressor/SZ3 v3.4.0, revision 592df793eb596d952242aa9fec9cbe5e68782aae.
https://github.com/szcompressor/SZ3

include/SZ3 holds only the headers of the 2D interpolation pipeline (SZGenericCompressor,
InterpolationDecomposition, LinearQuantizer, HuffmanEncoder and Lossless_bypass) and what they
include, with the local changes below. The public SZ_compress API, the other algorithms and Lossless_zstd are
left out: they require zstd. version.hpp is upstream version.hpp.in configured for 3.4.0.

The TWM raster profile (libs/indexer/terrain/sz3_profile.hpp) composes these modules directly
into a headerless frame and replaces the zstd stage with optional deflate. Like SPERR, the
reconstructed integer heights must match on all supported architectures: the encoder and the
decoder are built with strict floating point.

Local changes in def.hpp, HuffmanEncoder.hpp and InterpolationDecomposition.hpp retain the
Huffman table and bin storage, use direct 2D block traversal and integer interpolator dispatch, and
compute the grid levels with integer bit widths. The encoder runs them too; its output, the stream
layout and the reconstruction order are unchanged. Every source including SZ3 builds with
-fno-fast-math -ffp-contract=off (MSVC /fp:strict) and, on GCC/Clang, defines SZ3_ASSUME_STRICT_FP
next to these flags (libs/indexer/CMakeLists.txt, the indexer Xcode project). The definition removes
the volatile spills of nofma() in def.hpp without permitting FMA or reassociation; def.hpp rejects
fast math in every SZ3 translation unit, Clang's included.
